Actual CLI parser arguments for the discoverable Outcome query.

The CLI flattens this type into `work-item outcome`; interface discovery reads the same Clap command model.  Keep transport-specific MCP-only parameters outside this type.

Usage: ai-cockpit work-item outcome [OPTIONS] --repo <REPO> --id <ID>

Options:
      --repo <REPO>
          

      --id <ID>
          Canonical Work Item identifier.

      --delivery
          Request the immutable full archive delivery payload.

      --json
          Emit machine-readable JSON instead of the human handoff.

      --view <VIEW>
          Select the reader-first summary or complete human view.
          
          [default: summary]
          [possible values: summary, full]

      --language <LANGUAGE>
          Active conversation language for the human Outcome; adapters should pass it explicitly, with locale fallback only when omitted.
          
          [possible values: en, zh, zh-CN, ja]

      --display-timezone <DISPLAY_TIMEZONE>
          Optional IANA timezone for the human lifecycle display; persisted UTC facts remain unchanged.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
